---
/*
 * What a reader sees after asking for a sign-in link.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * IT CLAIMS A SEND, NOT A DELIVERY
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * All we know is that GoTrue accepted the request. Mail is queued, may be rate limited, and
 * may be filtered. "Check your inbox" states as fact something we have not observed, and this
 * repo has already shipped two claims of that shape (an install command that could not run,
 * and a backend the page said it had). So the heading says the link is on its way, and the
 * body tells the reader what to do when it is not there — which is the useful half anyway.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * THE ADDRESS IS ECHOED BACK
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * A typo in an email address is invisible at the moment you make it and expensive a minute
 * later, when nothing arrives and the obvious conclusion is that the product is broken.
 * Showing what we actually sent to lets the reader catch it themselves. The script fills
 * [data-email-sent-address] with the exact string that was submitted.
 *
 * It is rendered with `textContent`, never innerHTML: this is user-supplied text on a page
 * that has just been given to an unauthenticated stranger.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SPAM IS NAMED FIRST
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Not as an apology but because it is the single most likely reason a link "did not arrive",
 * and a person who has not been told to look there will conclude the send failed and try
 * again — which, on a rate-limited sender, is the one action that guarantees the second link
 * is slower than the first.
 */

import "./panel.css";
import Button from "../ui/Button.astro";
---

<section
  class="st-pn"
  data-panel="email-sent"
  tabindex="-1"
  aria-labelledby="pn-sent-t"
  hidden
>
  <h2 class="st-pn__t" id="pn-sent-t">Your sign-in link is on its way</h2>

  <p class="st-pn__p">
    We sent it to <strong class="st-pn__addr" data-email-sent-address></strong>. Open it on
    this device and you will land back here, signed in.
  </p>

  <p class="st-pn__p">
    The link signs you in once and then stops working. If it does not show up in a minute,
    check your spam folder — that is where it usually is.
  </p>

  <div class="st-pn__act">
    <Button data-resend size="lg" block variant="secondary">
      Use a different address
    </Button>
  </div>

  <p class="st-pn__soon-note">
    You can close this tab. The link works from your inbox on its own.
  </p>
</section>
